1. She has a professionally diagnosed agoraphobia, which involves fear of external environments where she feels a lack of control, not just crowds. (Verbatim: "I have professionally diagnosed with agoraphobia... it's a fear of being in sort of external environments where you don't have control.")

2. She finds long queues at theme parks extremely difficult, especially when they are outdoors and cold. (Verbatim: "The queues were very long... and it was really cold i was really really really cold i was freezing.")

3. She is terrified of roller coasters with loops and would need someone to hold onto if she ever attempted one. (Verbatim: "I haven't done any roller coasters before with a loop because that's way too scary... i need an arm to squeeze or a hand to squeeze onagai shimasu.")

4. She considers the roller coaster she recently rode (without loops) the scariest ride she has ever been on. (Verbatim: "I would say that's definitely the scariest ride i've been on.")

5. She wants to see the cherry blossoms in Japan and visit arcades to play rhythm and crane games. (Verbatim: "I want to see the cherry blossoms... i want to go to the arcade and play on the music rhythm games and i want to... do more crane games.")

6. She owns a Vaporeon plushie, which she recently purchased, and considered naming it "Vape-chan." (Verbatim: "I bought myself a plushie... it was vaporeon... what would i call it... vape chan.")

